		uses 73 and 74 for loads and stores resolved to fixed storage.
		The u64 type uses 54.
		87 through 90 select u64 masks and shifts, and 91 through 94 select u32 and u64 XOR and complement.
		An owner null predicate uses 98, optional unwrap uses 101, native:alloc uses 103, and native:empty uses 198.
		Integer byte conversions use 108 through 111, and typed checked conversions use 112.
		Enum and match forms use 113 through 117. Break and continue use 144 and 145.
		Signed i32 masks and shifts use 152 through 155.
		Exact-width arithmetic uses the range from source/integer_ops.wove.
		Recoverable integer checks use 188 through 193.
		i64 wrapping arithmetic uses 207 through 209. Integer comparisons
		use the encoded range from integer_compare.
